# A law (wiki/laws.md) is a hint, which wap verify tests and proves: a build runs none, and the program's value is its
# own, the short form `law square(-x) == square(x)` and a named one with its `for` lines alike, and one with binders,
# which sugar/definitions.wap reads as `law(positive: ((x: int) -> x > 0))`
# a law or a theorem with a proof is the function giving the proof (wiki/proof.md), which a program may call, claimed
# to do nothing but compute its value: a proof that may loop, raise or act is refused by the claim
# (core/analyze/effects.wap claims_checked). Its statement is checked by wap verify
# TODO (card rule-word-set) one rule each `where $word in [theorem, law]` once a rule's where takes more than one word
rule law($name($parameters...): $statement := $proof) => $name($parameters...): $statement := $proof ! Pure
rule law($name: $statement := $proof) => $name(): $statement := $proof ! Pure
rule theorem($name($parameters...): $statement := $proof) => $name($parameters...): $statement := $proof ! Pure
rule theorem($name: $statement := $proof) => $name(): $statement := $proof ! Pure
rule law $statement... => ()
rule law($statement) => ()
